  1086	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1087	# PLAN-094 Wave C — sentinel verification session cache (R-041)
  1088	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1089	# Module-scope ONLY (NEVER file-backed; PLAN-094 §3 Wave C C.1).
  1090	# Process death = cache loss (eliminates R5 stale-cache-survives-crash).
  1091	# Composite key — Codex iter-1 P0 fold: target_rel included so cache value
  1092	# (grant decision dependent on target_rel) is correct on hit; sha256_full
  1093	# transitively covers signer changes via .asc bytes (signer rotation
  1094	# window risk acknowledged + accepted trade-off per design draft §8).
  1095	
  1096	_SENTINEL_CACHE_FORMAT_VERSION = 2  # bumped at iter-1 P0 fix (target_rel added)
  1097	_SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE: Dict[
  1098	    Tuple[str, int, int, int, str, str, int], bool
  1099	] = {}
  1100	_SENTINEL_CACHE_HITS = 0
  1101	_SENTINEL_CACHE_MISSES = 0
  1102	
  1103	# PLAN162_FIX_1 (PLAN-162 findings #1 + #10, consensus C1 + C2 + C3 + S8).
  1104	#
  1105	# ## The defect (#1, re-diagnosed in debate: AMPLIFICATION, not latency)
  1106	#
  1107	# The cache above folds ``target_rel`` into its key, but
  1108	# ``_gpg_verify.verify_detached`` never RECEIVES a target — signature
  1109	# validity is target-INDEPENDENT. So the same sentinel was
  1110	# cryptographically re-verified once per distinct target: a subprocess
  1111	# count of O(candidates x sentinels). Measured in debate, gpg-agent
  1112	# healthy: 1 GPG ~ 17 ms, but a 20-path ceremony pack cost **4.16 s of a
  1113	# 5 s hook budget** with 0 cache hits and 320 misses (40 paths: 4.23 s).
  1114	#
  1115	# ## The fix — two caches, not one
  1116	#
  1117	#   * ``_SIG_VERIFY_CACHE`` — the SIGNATURE rail, keyed on the signing
  1118	#     MATERIAL and NOT on the target. 320 subprocesses collapse to 16.
  1119	#   * ``_GRANT_CACHE`` — the SCOPE rail, target-keyed and cheap. This is
  1120	#     the SAME object as ``_SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE`` (an alias, not a
  1121	#     copy): the PLAN-094 key shape and counters are pinned by
  1122	#     ``test_sentinel_session_cache.py`` and stay byte-compatible.
  1123	#
  1124	# ## Why the signature rail must run FIRST (this is finding #10)
  1125	#
  1126	# #10 observed that the grant key hashes only ``approved.md``'s bytes, so
  1127	# mutating the ``.asc`` / signer allowlist / ADR-121 registry left a
  1128	# stale ``True`` riding the cache in-process. Rather than smuggle a
  1129	# digest of three more files into a key shape other tests pin, the
  1130	# signature rail is consulted BEFORE the grant fast-path and keys on
  1131	# those bytes itself. A revocation in any of the three now invalidates
  1132	# the decision even when ``approved.md`` is byte-identical — closing the
  1133	# "signer rotation window" that PLAN-094 §8 had consciously accepted.
  1134	_SIG_CACHE_FORMAT_VERSION = 1
  1135	_SIG_VERIFY_CACHE: Dict[tuple, bool] = {}
  1136	_GRANT_CACHE = _SENTINEL_VERIFY_CACHE  # alias — same dict object
  1137	
  1138	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1139	# PLAN162_FIX_1 — per-invocation wall-clock budget (consensus C2 + C3 + S8)
  1140	# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1141	# C2 REMOVED the sentinel cap from the design: ``_find_sentinels`` returns
  1142	# SORTED, so the highest-numbered pack — the ceremony the Owner just
  1143	# signed — is exactly the sentinel a cap would drop. Self-DoS with the
  1144	# signature in hand, and it does not even fix a hung gpg (one hang costs
  1145	# the full timeout at cap=1). What replaces it is a global wall-clock
  1146	# deadline per INVOCATION, checked at the top of the sentinel loops.
  1147	#
  1148	# C3: the budget is a MODULE CONSTANT, never read from settings.json at
  1149	# runtime — the budget lives in the file this hook guards (circular), and
  1150	# parsing JSON on the hot path would worsen the very path being
  1151	# optimized. Drift against the registered timeout is a STATIC test
  1152	# instead (the shape verify-counts.sh already uses):
  1153	# ``test_1_repro_wall_deadline_constant_has_slack_under_registration``.
  1154	# 4.0 s under the registered 5 s leaves ~1 s to emit the decision.
  1155	#
  1156	# S8: the clock is an injectable module-level seam (``_now``). Without
  1157	# it the red-first test's only options were a multi-second real sleep
  1158	# (a documented flake class in this repo) or no deterministic coverage
  1159	# of the slow path at all. This is a requirement OF the fix.
  1160	#
     1	#!/bin/bash
     2	# =============================================================================
     3	# PLAN-169 W3 — LAND do pack canônico (Owner-run, DEPOIS do GA v1.3.0).
     4	#
     5	# ORDEM PINADA: este pack SÓ landa após o GA da v1.3.0 (W6.1) — durante o
     6	# hold de 24h, NENHUM commit em main. Conteúdo = v1.4.0.
     7	#
     8	# O que ele faz, nesta ordem, TUDO fail-closed:
     9	#   G0  main não está congelado (você confirma interativamente)
    10	#   G1  BASELINE anti-stale: cada alvo VIVO ainda é byte-idêntico ao que o
    11	#       pack viu no staging — se main andou por cima de um alvo, ABORTA
    12	#       (a lição do step1 do PLAN-166: staged stale reverte trabalho novo)
    13	#   G2  MANIFEST: shasum -c dos 12 staged (integridade do pack)
    14	#   G3  Sentinel GPG: W3-approved.md assinado + Scope cobre exatamente os
    15	#       alvos (touched − scope = ∅ é verificado APÓS o apply)
    16	#   G4  Simulação em clone: aplica o pack num git clone --local e roda a
    17	#       bateria (render 9/9 + pytest dos hooks tocados + INV-4) ANTES de
    18	#       tocar a árvore viva
    19	#   G5  Apply por TABELA (cp staged → vivo), preservando modo executável
    20	#   G6  touched − scope = ∅ + bateria na árvore viva + verify-counts
    21	#   G7  Commit (mensagem pronta) — push fica MANUAL (pre-push roda gates)
    22	#
    23	# Uso:  bash .claude/plans/PLAN-169/OWNER-W3-LAND.sh [--dry-run]
    24	#   --dry-run: para após G4 (nada toca a árvore viva).
