- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-RC3-CUT.sh:100` — Cure evidence and the staged pack are verified independently. `MANIFEST-cures.sha256` covers only round tuples; `PROVENANCE-cures.md` is merely allowed on disk, and G0 never checks that it names `EXPECTED_HEAD` or pins the current `staged-rc3/{MANIFEST,BASELINE}.sha256`. A stale GO evidence directory plus a different self-consistent pack therefore passes and is signed as reviewed. Minimal fix: record both pack-manifest hashes and the exact anchor in provenance, include provenance in `MANIFEST-cures.sha256`, and compare those fields exactly in G0.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:130` — GA evidence closure is name-only before `git add "$GA_DIR"` at line 195; unlike the rc.3/NOGO checks, it never rejects symlinks or other non-regular entries. An allowed-name symlink can redirect or collapse verdict/payload files, while `-f`, `shasum`, and the server guard follow it and `git add` commits the link. Minimal fix: reject every non-regular entry, forbid subdirectories, require exact direct-child set equality after the runner, and add the enumerated outputs rather than the directory.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:155` — The advertised GA resume path rejects its own partial signing state. After line 209 renders `$VF`, an invited Ctrl-C, failed pinentry, failed `sed`, or failed verdict commit leaves `$VF`, `$VF.asc`, or `$VD` dirty outside `GA_DIR`; the next G0 aborts. If the failed commit left VF/VD staged, a naïve retry could also sweep them into the evidence commit because line 195 tests the entire index. Minimal fix: quarantine/regenerate those exact artifacts on resume and make the evidence cached check/commit path-scoped to `GA_DIR`.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/repass-ga/run-ga-repass.sh:202` — The runner uses `set -uo pipefail`, but final `shasum` generation is unguarded. If it fails or writes a partial manifest while both Codex exits were zero, the script still exits with `OVERALL=0`; OWNER-GA proceeds through signing and commits until the later delta guard rejects it. Minimal fix: explicitly abort on manifest-generation failure and verify its exact set/content before returning zero.

- P1 — `.claude/plans/PLAN-166/OWNER-GA-CUT.sh:283` — The post-tag release wait remains 40 minutes although `release-gate` alone may consume 35 minutes and `publish-release` runs afterward. A valid slow run can exceed 40 minutes, aborting after the GA tag was pushed; rerun is then refused because the tag exists. Minimal fix: raise the budget to at least 55–60 minutes and permit monitoring resume when the existing local/remote tag resolves exactly to the expected HEAD.

For the stated four-round cure set, the template basenames, delta-manifest set, and reused `inputs_hash` are otherwise coherent with the guard and step-15 validator.

